# Keep the build context small and the image reproducible.
#
# Anything listed here is either a build product that the container regenerates, a
# machine-specific artefact, or a document that has no business inside a runtime
# image. A smaller context also means faster rebuilds, since Docker hashes it on
# every `build`.

# --- version control and tooling ---
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Python build products ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- environment and secrets ---
# GROQ_API_KEY reaches the container through docker-compose environment, never
# through a file baked into the image.
.env
*.key

# --- build products the container regenerates itself ---
pipeline/index/
logs/*.db
logs/*.db-journal
logs/*.jsonl
logs/queries/
corpus/sources/cache/

# The fitted model is bind-mounted from the host so `fusion.train` can write it back.
# Excluding it from the context keeps a stale copy from being baked into the image.
fusion/artifacts/*.joblib
fusion/artifacts/*.pkl

# --- generated documents ---
# The Markdown sources are copied; the binaries are regenerated on demand and would
# add several megabytes to every layer.
*.docx
*.pdf
~$*

# --- evaluation output ---
# Bind-mounted from the host, so a copy in the image would be immediately shadowed
# and could mislead anyone inspecting the image directly.
eval/results/

# --- editor and OS noise ---
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Docker's own files ---
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore

# --- stray output directories ---
Claude outputs/
